{"name":"Outer Boundary","hex":"#654846","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"outer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Outside; external.","Farther from the centre of the inside."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outer part.","An uncovered section of the seating at a stadium or sportsground."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outer"},{"term":"boundary","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The dividing line or location between two areas.","The bounds, confines, or limits between immaterial things (such as one’s comfort zone, privacy, or professional sphere and the realm beyond)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boundary"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boundary (graph theory)","blocks":[{"text":"In graph theory, the outer boundary of a subset S of the vertices of a graph G is the set of vertices in G that are adjacent to vertices in S, but not in S themselves. The inner boundary is the set of vertices in S that have a neighbor outside S. The edge boundary is the set of edges with one endpoint in the inner boundary and one endpoint in the outer boundary."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boundary_(graph_theory)","wikidata":"Q106371443"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"outer":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ae/En-uk-outta.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/ae/En-uk-outta.ogg/En-uk-outta.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a2/En-us-outer.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a2/En-us-outer.ogg/En-us-outer.ogg.mp3"}],"boundary":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/63/En-us-boundary.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/63/En-us-boundary.ogg/En-us-boundary.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cd/En-au-boundary.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/cd/En-au-boundary.ogg/En-au-boundary.ogg.mp3"}]}}}